// ===================================================================
// BASIC BROS RYDER CUP — CLOUD FIRESTORE SECURITY RULES
//
// Paste the whole contents of this file into:
//   Firebase console -> Build -> Firestore Database -> Rules tab
//   then click Publish.
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS EVEN THOUGH THE SITE DOES NOT USE FIRESTORE:
//
// The site stores everything in Realtime Database (see
// database.rules.json). Firestore was switched on early in the build,
// in "test mode", and then never used. An empty Firestore database in
// test mode is still wide open to the whole internet, and Google emails
// a warning about that every day until it is locked down or deleted.
//
// These rules slam it shut. Nothing can read it, nothing can write to
// it, which is correct: no part of the site talks to Firestore.
//
// If you would rather remove Firestore from the project entirely, you
// can delete the database in the console instead — Firestore Database
// -> the "..." menu next to the database name -> Delete database. Both
// options stop the emails. Publishing these rules is the safer one,
// because it is instantly reversible.
// ===================================================================

rules_version = '2';

service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {

    // Deny everything, at every path. No exceptions.
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}
